 Scroll left one screen width.
 .TP
@@ -498,6 +540,28 @@ Please see xrdb(1) on how to change them.
 .LP
 An X resources entry with an empty value means the default
 (defined in config.h) will be used.
+.SH WALLPAPER
+The wallpaper is rendered to a pixmap the size of the screen, installed as the
+root window background and published through the
+.I _XROOTPMAP_ID
+and
+.I ESETROOT_PMAP_ID
+properties, so compositors and pseudo-transparent terminals can pick it up. The
+pixmap is retained by the X server after nsxiv exits, and the one from a
+previous wallpaper is released when it is replaced.
+.P
+Unless
+.B \-\-no\-bgscript
+is given, nsxiv also writes
+.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nsxiv/nsxivbg
+(or
+.I ~/.config/nsxiv/nsxivbg
+if
+.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
+is unset), a shell script that restores the last wallpaper. It is the
+counterpart of feh's
+.IR ~/.fehbg ,
+and can be run from your X startup file.
 .SH WINDOW TITLE
 The window title can be replaced with the output of a user-provided script,
 which is called by nsxiv whenever any of the relevant information changes.
